<task id="245a" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Run context, part 1 (G25) — every handler input declared with one producer: H2a persists its ARM outputs, consumers read typed state, closed intake catalog at POST /api/runs, H4b closed per-env source catalog, DAG gaps closed, forcing-function test</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T245 (G25, notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies production .cs in Api + Core (H2a, H3, H4, H4b, H9, H12b, H13, H14, DagAdvancer, RunsEndpoints, InterStepState), adds a forcing-function test, updates many handler test fixtures; root §8 test-modifying override applies.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting refactor of the handler data-flow contract across 8+ handlers plus a new contract abstraction and a DAG change (high blast radius, architectural).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/ (constraints + pattern pointer) — main-session-only; also shares InterStepState / DagAdvancer / RunsEndpoints with T245b/T245c/T238 (sequential by design)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none (T226 ✅, T237 ✅)</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, l2-controlplane, provisioning-handler, api, endpoints, testing, config, customer-provisioning</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    A real provisioning run cannot get past H0 because ~20 required handler inputs are read from
    `run.Parameters.NonSecret`, which only the intake copy ever writes. Establish the run-context contract — every
    value a handler reads has exactly one declared source (intake, run identity, or a typed handler output written by
    a handler that runs earlier) — and move every customer-stamp value H2a already receives from ARM into typed
    `InterStepState`, so H3/H4/H4b/H9/H12b/H13/H14 stop reading values nobody writes. Inputs owned by T245b (L2-owned
    values) and T245c (operator intake additions) are declared as known gaps that this task's test pins.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer on the L2 provisioning control plane. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in C#/.NET 10,
    System.Text.Json, ARM deployment outputs, xUnit + FluentAssertions fitness-function tests.
  </role>

  <goal>
    After this task: (1) H2a writes resource group, App Service name, staging slot name, Key Vault name + URI, UAMI
    resource id and Service Bus FQNS to `InterStepState`; (2) H3, H4, H4b, H9, H12b, H13 and H14 read those values (and
    H5's `DataverseEnvUrl`) from `InterStepState`, never from `Parameters.NonSecret`; (3) `POST /api/runs` accepts only
    keys in a closed intake catalog and defaults/validates `environmentName`; (4) H4b resolves `per_env_settings` sources
    through a closed catalog; (5) the DAG makes every required handler-output producer an ancestor of its reader; (6) a
    test fails if any handler reads an input that has no declared producer — except the pinned known gaps owned by
    T245b/T245c.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Evidence: notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md (audit 2026-09-30). The only production write to
      `Parameters.NonSecret` is `RunsEndpoints.cs:645`. H2a already maps ResourceGroupName, AppServiceName,
      AppServiceStagingSlotName and UserAssignedIdentityResourceId from ARM (`BicepDeployOutputs.cs:29-60`,
      `ArmDeploymentRunner.cs:465-479`) but persists only five fields (`H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs:797-801`).
      `customer.bicep` outputs `keyVaultName`, `keyVaultUri` (:796-797) and `serviceBusEndpoint` (:808, shape
      `https://{ns}.servicebus.windows.net:443/`) — unmapped. The H4b `per_env_settings` sources in
      `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml:676-863` are snake_case keys nothing writes; two of them mislabel
      their origin (`from-h0-parameter:tenant_id` and `from-h8-output:container_type_id` are intake values). H4b depends
      only on H4 (`DagAdvancer.cs:151`) although it needs H3's `BffAppRegId`; H6 reads `BffAppRegId` but depends only on
      H5 (:152); H7 reads `SpeContainerId` (H8 output) but depends only on H6 (:153). H2a's name-availability check builds
      the Service Bus name `sprk-{id}-{env}-sb` (`H2a:659`) while `customer.bicep:177` names it `spaarke-{id}-{env}-sbus`.
      `environmentName` is silently defaulted to "prod" by H2a (:319) and H2b (:302) but required with no default by
      H4b; nothing sends it. D6: customer stamps are prod-only for now.
      SECOND CHANNEL — `run.Parameters.Secrets` (KeyVaultSecretRef map): H4's manifest-driven resolver reads it for
      `from-run-parameter` / `from-existing-kv` entries (`KvSecretValueResolver.cs:231-250`) — `TenantId`,
      `BFF-API-ClientId`, `BFF-API-Audience` (manifest.yaml:126-235). The only writer is H3 on consent-verified success
      (`H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs:653-659`), but H3 depends on H4 (`DagAdvancer.cs:150`, H3 needs H4's KV RBAC bootstrap),
      so H4 can never see them: every real run fails at H4 and resuming cannot help — a deadlock. H3 already commits
      BFF-API-ClientId / BFF-API-Audience to the customer vault itself (`GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs:223-227`),
      and nothing supplies a `TenantId` reference (the tenant id is a non-secret intake value).
      Model 1 still routes to `model1-shared.bicep`, whose outputs use different names (T225a/T225b converge it); after
      this task a Model 1 run fails `BicepDeployOutputsIncomplete` at H2a exactly as it already fails today — no
      regression, and no Model 1 template work in this task.
    </background>
