  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project (this task's contract — BINDING)">
      Every input a handler in this repo reads comes from exactly one of: (a) the run's top-level identity
      (`CustomerId`, `TenancyModel`, `Profile`, `EnvironmentId`); (b) an intake key in `IntakeParameterCatalog`, read
      from `Parameters.NonSecret`; (c) a typed `InterStepState` property whose `[ProducedBy]` handler is a strict
      transitive DAG ancestor of the reader (required inputs) — optional reads (e.g. H4's leak scan) are exempt from
      the ancestor rule but still declared. No handler may read a handler-produced value from `Parameters.NonSecret`.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="project — known gaps">
      Inputs whose source is decided by T245b or T245c stay as they are in code and are declared as known gaps with the
      owning task id. The exact known-gap set is pinned by `RunContextContractTests` (adding or removing one is a test
      edit). T245a does not implement T245b/T245c scope: artifact versions (`bicepVer`, `indexVer`, `secretsVer`), the
      SPE owner-certificate vault (H0 probe, H8, T6 probe), H9 outputs (`bffApiUrl`, `buildId`) and H14
      `webhookNotificationBaseUrl` → T245b; H11 `identityPreset`/`usersJson`, H14 `exchangePolicyScopeGroupId` +
      Graph resources → T245c.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 + project boundary">
      No change to `Sprk.Bff.Api` or `infrastructure/bicep/**` (H2a derives the Service Bus FQNS from the existing
      `serviceBusEndpoint` output by URI host — it does not compose names). The control plane MUST NOT reference the BFF.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001 / ADR-008 / .claude/constraints/api.md">
      CreateRun rejections use the endpoint's existing `BadRequest(httpContext, ...)` ProblemDetails helper and run
      before the registry lookup, CustomerRunGuard, Cosmos write and enqueue (same placement as the T237 checks).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">
      New types are static catalogs / attributes / records — no new interfaces or DI registrations unless a second
      implementation exists.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7 + tests/CLAUDE.md">
      Handler tests that seeded `NonSecret` keys for values now read from `InterStepState` are changed to seed
      `InterStepState`; no test is deleted, skipped or weakened. Missing-input tests keep asserting the same rejection
      code for the same missing value (now absent from `InterStepState`). No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="manifest generator contract">
      `per_env_source` strings keep the generator's grammar `from-{origin}-{output|parameter}:{key}`; changed origins
      are `from-intake-parameter:tenant_id` and `from-intake-parameter:container_type_id`. `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1
      -Verify` passes after regeneration; the generated script's parameter names do not change.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-11 / no live changes">
      No live Azure or Dataverse change in this task.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

