  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add `ProducedByAttribute(string handlerId)` and `NoProducerAttribute(string reason)` (Core/Models). Annotate every `InterStepState` property with exactly one: BffAppRegId/FicPendingPostAppServiceVerification ← H3; MiObjectId/MiClientId/OpenAiEndpoint/AiSearchEndpoint/CosmosEndpoint ← H2a; DataverseEnvUrl ← H5; ImportedSolutions ← H6; SpeContainerId ← H8; SystemUserId/BffAppRegSystemUserId ← H10; ProvisionedUsers ← H11; S2SAppRegId, ContainerTypeId, SpeConsentCorrelationId → `[NoProducer]` with the reason (legacy guard / intake value / Model 2 H0.5 out of scope). Add H2a-produced properties: ResourceGroupName, AppServiceName, AppServiceStagingSlotName, KeyVaultName, KeyVaultUri, MiResourceId, ServiceBusFullyQualifiedNamespace (JSON camelCase names, WhenWritingNull).</step>
    <step order="2">H2a: extend `BicepDeployOutputs` with KeyVaultName, KeyVaultUri, ServiceBusFullyQualifiedNamespace (required); `ArmDeploymentRunner.MapOutputs` reads `keyVaultName`, `keyVaultUri`, and derives the FQNS as the host of `serviceBusEndpoint` (blank if absent/unparseable → existing BicepDeployOutputsIncomplete). H2a writes all seven new properties next to the existing five. Fix `BuildGloballyNamespacedNameChecks` to check `spaarke-{id}-{env}-sbus` (customer.bicep:177).</step>
    <step order="3">Add `IntakeParameterCatalog`: the closed set of intake keys (every key the skill sends at SKILL.md Step 4.0 + every optional override a handler reads today that is genuinely operator/intake-owned + `environmentName`), each with required/optional and a one-line description. `CreateRun`: 400 for any key not in the catalog (message lists the unknown keys); `environmentName` absent → store "prod" in the run's NonSecret; present but not dev|staging|prod → 400. Existing tenantId/subscriptionId checks stay. H2a/H2b drop their silent "prod" defaults (missing → Resumable failure with a clear code; unreachable after CreateRun).</step>
    <step order="4">Switch consumers to typed state: H3 (customer KV), H4 (KV, RG, App Service, UAMI resource id, staging slot), H4b (KV, RG, App Service), H9 (RG, App Service, staging slot), H12b (`DataverseEnvUrl`), H13 (RG, App Service, KV — now required; containerTypeId from intake, no ISS fallback), H14 (KV). Remove the now-unused `*ParameterKey` constants for those values. Keep each handler's existing rejection code for the missing value; update the diagnostic text to name the producing handler.</step>
    <step order="5">H4b: add `PerEnvSourceCatalog` — closed map from `per_env_source` string to (origin, resolver over the run): `from-h2a-output:kv_vault_uri`→KeyVaultUri, `from-h2a-output:cosmos_endpoint`→CosmosEndpoint, `from-h2a-output:uami_client_id`→MiClientId, `from-h2a-output:service_bus_fqns`→ServiceBusFullyQualifiedNamespace, `from-h3-output:bff_app_client_id`→BffAppRegId, `from-intake-parameter:tenant_id`→intake `tenantId`, `from-intake-parameter:container_type_id`→intake `containerTypeId`. An unknown source string fails the manifest read (`FilePerEnvSettingsManifest`). Update the two mislabelled `per_env_source` strings in manifest.yaml; regenerate; `-Verify`. Fix the "envelope.Parameters.NonSecret" misnomers in H4b / IPerEnvSettingsManifest / manifest comments.</step>
    <step order="6">DAG (`DagAdvancer.HandlerDependencies`): H4b ← {H4, H3}; H6 ← {H5, H3}; H7 ← {H6, H8}. Confirm no cycle; update DagAdvancerTests / Model1SharedDagParityTests rows.</step>
    <step order="6b">Secrets channel (H3 ↔ H4 deadlock): give every H4 manifest entry a producer that runs before H4 or is H4 itself. `TenantId` is written from the intake `tenantId` value (a non-secret source in the manifest's closed value_source set — extend the set + generator + FileKvSecretManifest + resolver if needed, same discipline as T226). `BFF-API-ClientId` / `BFF-API-Audience` are produced by H3's own KV commit: mark them in the manifest as written by H3 and make H4 skip (not fail) entries another handler writes; H3 no longer writes `run.Parameters.Secrets` refs for them. Declare `Parameters.Secrets` reads/writes in HandlerRunInputs and cover them in the contract test (rule (e) scans `Parameters.Secrets[...]` too).</step>
    <step order="7">Add `HandlerRunInputs` (one static table: handler id → declared inputs: Identity / Intake(key, required) / Output(InterStepState property, required) / KnownGap(name, owningTask)). Add `RunContextContractTests`: (a) every InterStepState property has exactly one of [ProducedBy]/[NoProducer] and every [ProducedBy] id is a real handler id; (b) every required Output input's producer is a strict transitive DAG ancestor of the reader; (c) every Intake key is in the catalog; (d) a [NoProducer] property is never a required input; (e) SOURCE SCAN — for each handler's folder under Core/Handlers (explicit folder→handler map in the test), every `InterStepState.{Prop}` read and every `const string ...ParameterKey = "..."` value is declared for that handler, and every `InterStepState.{Prop} =` assignment is in its [ProducedBy] handler's folder; (f) the KnownGap set equals a pinned list. Failure messages name handler + input + rule.</step>
    <step order="8">Docs: `.claude/constraints/provisioning.md` rule (declare every new handler input in HandlerRunInputs; never read a handler output from NonSecret); `.claude/patterns/provisioning/run-context-contract.md` 25-line pointer + INDEX row; `.claude/CHANGELOG.md`; design.md §6.2 key list + §4.1 DAG rows; notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md §5 "T245a done" + remaining gaps.</step>
    <step order="9">Build + run ControlPlane.Tests, LoadTests compile, ArchTests; `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify`; prereqs validate.ps1.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md row 245a to `✅ [done]`, POML status completed, plan §3/§4/§7 rows.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a handler input cannot be classified as identity / intake / typed handler output / T245b-T245c known gap without an owner decision (e.g. a value that would need a new operator prompt), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than inventing a source.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a DAG change in step 6 creates a cycle, or any change alters Model 2 / H0.5 behaviour, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If rejecting unknown intake keys would break a caller other than the skill, RunsEndpointsTests or the two LoadTests scenarios, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If resolving the H3 ↔ H4 secrets deadlock requires splitting H4 into two handlers or reordering H3 before H4 (H3 needs H4's KV RBAC bootstrap), STOP and escalate with the options — that is a DAG redesign, not a source fix.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Producer/consumer contract today exists only as prose in InterStepState.cs ("Handlers write once; downstream handlers read") and per-handler "upstream MUST populate" comments; `HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests` checks registration, not data flow (grep "ProducedBy|RunInputs|IntakeParameter" → none).</existing>
    <extension>The new types extend InterStepState (attributes) and DagAdvancer's existing dependency map (the test reads it); a declared-inputs table cannot be expressed by extending either, because the inputs are per-handler facts that neither type holds.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A real run fails at H0 and every later handler with a value nobody writes; the next handler author adds another unproduced NonSecret key and unit tests stay green because they seed it by hand — exactly how G25 happened. PerEnvSourceCatalog: without it an unknown/mislabelled per_env_source resolves to a missing key at runtime instead of failing at manifest load.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Run the catalog generator and prereqs validator</tool>
  </tools>

