  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a deployment whose outputs carry keyVaultName, keyVaultUri, serviceBusEndpoint and the existing outputs, when H2a completes, then InterStepState holds ResourceGroupName, AppServiceName, AppServiceStagingSlotName, KeyVaultName, KeyVaultUri, MiResourceId and ServiceBusFullyQualifiedNamespace (= host of serviceBusEndpoint); given any of the three new outputs is missing, H2a returns the existing BicepDeployOutputsIncomplete code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a run whose NonSecret has NO keyVaultName/resourceGroupName/appServiceName/userAssignedIdentityResourceId/dataverseUrl but whose InterStepState carries the H2a/H5 outputs, H3, H4, H4b (up to its known-gap secretsVer check), H9, H12b, H13 (up to its known-gap buildId check) and H14 (up to its known-gap checks) get past every input guard for those values; given the InterStepState value is absent, each returns its existing rejection code for that value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/runs with a nonSecretParameters key outside the catalog returns 400 naming the key, with no registry lookup, Cosmos write or enqueue; with environmentName absent the stored run has environmentName=prod; with environmentName=demo returns 400; the skill's current 11-key payload is accepted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H4b resolves all seven per_env sources from the run (InterStepState / intake) and passes them as script arguments; a manifest with an unknown per_env_source string fails the manifest read (ManifestReadFailed); the real embedded manifest loads through the catalog.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DagAdvancer: H4b becomes ready only after H4 and H3; H6 only after H5 and H3; H7 only after H6 and H8; no cycle.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a run with NO `Parameters.Secrets` entries (state before H3 has run), H4 resolves `TenantId` from the intake tenantId, skips BFF-API-ClientId / BFF-API-Audience as H3-written, and does not fail on them; given the real embedded manifest, `Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify` passes and an unknown value_source still fails the manifest read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RunContextContractTests rules (a)–(f) pass; deliberately adding an undeclared `InterStepState.X` read or an undeclared `...ParameterKey` constant to a handler file makes rule (e) fail naming the file (verify once by hand, then revert).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify passes; prereqs validate.ps1 passes; ControlPlane builds 0 errors / 0 warnings; ControlPlane.Tests has no new failures beyond the 6-test T221 baseline; LoadTests compile; ArchTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the contract rules and the behaviours named above (H2a mapping incl. missing-output case, each switched consumer's present/absent path, CreateRun unknown-key / environmentName default / invalid, per-env catalog resolve + unknown-source, DAG readiness). Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Source scan in rule (e) reads handler source files located from the repo root (walk up from the test
    assembly to the directory holding `.git`). H0 probes live under Handlers/Preflight and belong to H0 in the folder map.

    COMPLETION (2026-10-01, SESSION 28/29). All acceptance criteria verified: ControlPlane.Tests 2063 pass / 6 fail
    (the T221 CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests baseline) / 1 skip; RunContextContractTests 30/30; ArchTests
    337/337; Api, Worker, LoadTests build 0/0; Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify OK; customer.json rebuilt.
    Rule (e) verified by hand: a seeded `_ = run.InterStepState?.CosmosEndpoint;` in H9 failed it naming
    "Handlers/BffDeploy (H9) reads InterStepState.CosmosEndpoint", then was removed.

    DEVIATIONS (each deliberate; reviewer-visible):
    (a) Step 3 — environmentName: one shared IntakeParameterCatalog.ResolveEnvironmentName (default `prod`, owner D6)
        for H2a/H2b/H4b instead of making H2a/H2b fail; CreateRun also stores the default. The
        `h4b-missing-environment-name` rejection code is retired (it can no longer occur) despite "keep existing
        rejection codes". A stored invalid value is not re-validated by handlers: customer.bicep's @allowed list fails
        it at H2a, which precedes H2b/H4b.
    (b) Step 6b — found 10 Secrets-channel consumers, not 3. Fixed: TenantId (`from-intake-parameter`),
        BFF-API-ClientId/Audience (`written-by-h3`; H3 no longer writes run.Parameters.Secrets). The rest are pinned in
        PinnedManifestGaps with owners (T245b, T245c, T225b; the two SPE container ids → T227/G18, found by the gates).
        The scan covers Parameters.Secrets as step 6b asked, as a rule rather than HandlerRunInputs entries: nobody may
        write it; only H4 may read it (RunSecretsReaders, with its reason).
    (c) Added: T6 trap probe reads TrapVerificationRequest.SpeOwnerCertKeyVaultName (platform vault, interim from intake
        `keyVaultName`); H13 passes the CUSTOMER vault as KeyVaultName (correct for T1/T5).
    (d) Rename TopologyConstantValues → IntakeValues across H4 / writer / resolver.
    (e) IntakeParameter.Key → Name (the FR-27 ArchTest treats a string property named Key as secret-shaped).
    (f) The scanner is a Roslyn syntax walk, not the regex the POML named (Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp 5.9.0 added
        to the L2 TEST project only). The regex scan had one comment bug found by its own producer-truthfulness check
        and three more found by code review (string literals, `?.`/`!.`, raw/verbatim strings), and was blind to the
        aliased reads six handlers use. Added beyond the POML: declared ⇒ read (stale declarations fail), literal intake
        keys beside the NonSecret map, rule (g) checked against customer.bicep's kvSecretValues, rule (h) generator ⇔
        PerEnvSourceCatalog parity, and negative + positive controls for every rule (tests/CLAUDE.md).
    (g) LoadTests request bodies fixed (pre-broken: T224-retired tenancy values, no tenantId).
    (h) H13: three new required-input codes `h13-missing-{resource-group,app-service,key-vault}-name`.
    (i) infrastructure/bicep/customer.json changed despite "no change to infrastructure/bicep/**": a regeneration
        (contentType tags from the regenerated kv-secrets module) plus one comment edit in customer.bicep (JSON unchanged).
    (j) Test deleted: H3EntraAppRegHandlerTests.AcParse_KvUriReference_RoundTrips — the production ParseKvUriReference
        it tested was removed as dead code; the H3 happy path now asserts Parameters.Secrets is empty.
    (k) Quality-gate fixes beyond the POML (owner: fix at discovery):
        - ADR-019: every control-plane ProblemDetails now carries a stable `errorCode` (Api/ControlPlaneProblems.cs,
          one helper for RunsEndpoints + RunLogsEndpoints); the unknown-key 400 returns `acceptedKeys`.
        - H4 cleartext-leak guard flagged real Azure host names (would have quarantined every real run at H4); it now
          exempts DNS hosts, scans URI path/query/user-info, and reflects over every InterStepState string property.
        - H13 sprk_azuresubscriptionid ← `subscriptionId` (the `azureSubscriptionId` intake key is removed); H13's literal
          intake keys became *ParameterKey constants.
        - New pinned T245b gaps: H7 `bffApiBaseUrl` (falls back to the PLATFORM BFF), H13 `bffVersion` /
          `solutionVersion` / `clientCacheBustToken`. T245b POML step 4c also carries the H4 KV-bootstrap principal
          defect (grants the stamp UAMI Secrets Officer instead of L2's principal) for owner review.
        - /provision-environment skill: `Model2Dedicated` comparisons (dead since T223/T224) now test `Model2`; the
          "L2 ignores unknown keys" comment replaced; Step 1c literals corrected; Step 5 gate note for the new edges.
        - Generator mirrors the closed per_env_source set (-Verify fails on a mislabelled source).
        - PerEnvSourceCatalog trims intake values like H4/H8; ArmDeploymentRunner.MapOutputs and H2a.MissingOutputs
          back to private (no test needed them); unused EnvironmentNameParameterKey constants removed (H2a, H2b).
    (l) ADR tensions recorded in spec.md: ADR-020 (strict intake reader, no deprecation window — path A) and
        ADR-038 (L2 fitness functions off the KEEP paths — path A, deletion-protected by that row).
    (m) DAG edges H4b←H3, H6←H3, H7←H8 apply to Model 2 as well; they only add true data dependencies (Model 2 is out
        of scope; H0.5 untouched).
    Test-scope justification: AC1b (H4b, every catalog source end-to-end) and AC28b–e (leak guard) cover the two
    production defects the gates found; the scanner controls are required by tests/CLAUDE.md. Four new tests that fed
    keys CreateRun now rejects were removed or narrowed to the reachable case (H9 AC2c2, H12b DataverseUrlOnlyInNonSecret,
    H13 AC2fgh rows, H4 keyVaultResourceId override).
  </notes>

